{"name":"Paint the Town Red","hex":"#e63045","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paint the town red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To party or celebrate in a rowdy, wild manner, especially in a public place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paint_the_town_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Mahones","blocks":[{"text":"The Mahones are a Canadian Irish punk band, formed on St. Patrick's Day in 1990, in Kingston, Ontario."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mahones.jpg/330px-Mahones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mahones","wikidata":"Q93625"},{"title":"Paint the Town Red (Delirious? song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Paint The Town Red\" is a single from and the tenth track on Delirious?'s album, The Mission Bell. It was released on 10 October 2005 to iTunes UK and the two high street music stores Virgin and HMV. The single entered the UK Singles Chart at No. 56. This was their lowest hit ever, and the first not to reach the UK Top 40 since \"White Ribbon Day\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Paint_The_Town_Red.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint_the_Town_Red_(Delirious%3F_song)","wikidata":"Q7124976"},{"title":"Paint the Town Red (Doja Cat song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Paint the Town Red\" is a song by American rapper and singer Doja Cat from her fourth studio album, Scarlet (2023). It was released on August 4, 2023, through Kemosabe and RCA Records as the lead single from the album. The song was written by Doja Cat and produced by Earl on the Beat, Rubin, Jean-Baptiste, and DJ Replay. The track samples Dionne Warwick's 1964 song \"Walk on By\". In the lyrics, the rapper dismisses her critics and asserts her own identity following arguments with fans on social media."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/53/Doja_Cat_-_Paint_the_Town_Red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint_the_Town_Red_(Doja_Cat_song)","wikidata":"Q121167968"},{"title":"Paint the Town","blocks":[{"text":"Paint the Town is the third studio album by American country music band Highway 101. The last of their albums featuring Paulette Carlson as lead vocalist, it included the Billboard Country #1 \"Who's Lonely Now,\" the #4 \"Walkin', Talkin', Cryin', Barely Beatin' Broken Heart,\" and the #11 \"This Side of Goodbye.\" Also included on the album is a cover of James Taylor's \"Sweet Baby James\". \"Rough and Tumble Heart\" was later recorded by Pam Tillis on her 1992 album Homeward Looking Angel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Highway101PainttheTown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paint_the_Town","wikidata":"Q7124975"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mahones.jpg/500px-Mahones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mahones.jpg/1280px-Mahones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Mahones.jpg/500px-Mahones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMahones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Paint_The_Town_Red.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Paint_The_Town_Red.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaint_The_Town_Red.jpeg"